---
description: Unity architecture rules for this project
alwaysApply: true
---

All project rules live in `.ai/AGENTS.md`. Read it before suggesting code, then open only the parts its routing table names for your task.

Non-negotiable, in case nothing else is loaded:

- Strict MVC: Models know only Models. Views know only Models and rendering components. Controllers know only Models and input interfaces.
- Events are `public event Action OnSomethingChanged;` with no parameters. Listeners pull from the Model.
- No `Button`, `Toggle`, `Slider` or `Dropdown`. Controllers implement `IPointer*` interfaces.
- Packages are optional. Read the project profile, `Logs/ai/profile.md` (run `bash scripts/ai-profile.sh` if it's missing), instead of reading the manifest. Where a rule depends on a package, its document has a fork: open only the file of the branch the profile names, never the others (`OPT-06`).
- Models have no serialized fields and form no cycles. Add no abstraction without a second use or a test need.
- Never write `.prefab`, `.unity`, `.asset` or `.meta` files as text. With a Unity MCP server or the Unity CLI, build them through editor tools.
- A change is verified only by a tool: the Console through Unity MCP, or `scripts/verify.sh`. Report anything else as not verified. See `.ai/architecture/EDITOR_TOOLS.md`.
